{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed","id":1536102,"title":"[Homebrew Legacy] The Changed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-22T10:12:12-07:00","id":1536102,"title":"[Homebrew Legacy] The Changed","content":"I created this legacy for a crossover chronicle but never quite finished it, I'm posting it here to share and ask for inspiration on the last 2 attainments.<br /> <br /> This is a changeling the lost crossover legacy. I tried to make the attainments so the awakened could participate into some activities changelings partake but to not step on their toes too much.<br /> 4th attainment would probably be something that can facilitate the mage into joining a Court and getting Court Goodwill, but I'm having a hard time making a Mind spell for the first part.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Changed</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Parentage:</b> Any, usually Acanthus<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> An Awakened Soul could not be so easily broken, but can be shaped by the ancient horrors that changelings call Keepers. This Legacy traces its origins back to an Awakened who has lost her name to a Fae being, and after being imprisoned in Arcadia, discovered that with enough practice, the Wyrd rules can be translated to Supernal ones. Using this knowledge, she escaped, returning to the Fallen World a changed person.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Members of this Legacy tend to have a vacant look in their eyes, as though they\u2019re always looking inwards at their own minds, half-remembering things. They often favor clothes of muted tones and subtle patterns, drawing inspiration from traditional practices of meditation and introspection. Some cultivate a particular style of clothing, such as a long coat or a simple robe, with subtle charms sewn into it. Some developed telltale signs of fae creature like pointed ears, heterochromia or a sixth finger because of the strange influences of the Hedge.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mind 2, Occult 2 and one of the following additional Skills at 2 dots or higher: Survival, Larceny, Empathy, Persuasion or Subterfuge.<br /> <b>Initiation:</b> A prospective member must have somehow got lost on the Hedge and made back into the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> This Legacy is rarely practiced as a cohesive group. Members tend to work in solitude and often as solo practitioners, preferring their own company to that of other mages. The only time these mages seek others is when other Awakened accidentally end up inside the Hedge. Is it not that the Legacy has a very strong tradition of secrecy, but that it came to be out of necessity. Members too far into the Legacy rarely if ever share information about their identity with other mages, lest they become the Obsession of their peers. Mages of this Legacy will never betray a promise made, and sometimes even participate in some Changeling courts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Mind<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Succeeding on an Hedge chase(+2); making a promise (+1); accruing a point of Goblin debt (+1); consuming Goblin fruits (+1, or +2 if the fruit creates an adverse Condition).<br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Hiding objects in intricate manner and places; daydreaming; rescuing someone; helping someone overcome mental trauma.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Legacy Attainments:</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>First: Recollection of Dreams<br /> Prerequisites: </b>Initiation<br /> The mage learns to tap into the depths of their memory, dredging up forgotten experiences and gleaning wisdom from long-lost dreams. Their mind becomes a vast library, holding not just facts and figures, but also the emotions and sensations of their past. This function as the Perfect Recall spell, with reach assigned for instant casting.<br /> <b>Optional Fate 1: </b>By remembering not just the details of their past, but also the emotions they felt, the mage learns to overcome even the most daunting challenges. This knowledge empowers them to face the unknown with confidence, this act like the Serendipity spell, with reach assigned for instant casting.<br /> <br /> <b>Second: Mr. Sandman<br /> Prerequisites: </b>Mind 2, Occult 3<br /> The Awakened learns how to access new realms. Utilizing the Astral Path rules(MtAw p248) she can leave her Bastion and enter the Dreaming Roads, where she can search for another Bastion and try to force entry or continue walking on her Astral Path until the Gates of Horn, arriving at the Hedge where she now must engage into a Hedge Chase. Her Shadow Name behaves strangely on these realms, with well know shadow names like Zeus making the character closely resemble the Greek God of Thunder archetype for example.<br /> <b>Optional Fate 2:</b> As a traveler of new realms, the mage quickly learns the rules of those places, least she suffer at the hands of it's inhabitants. This function as the Interconnections spell, with reach assigned for instant casting and to detect possession, supernatural mind control or alterations of destiny.<br /> <br /> <b>Third: The Weaver\u2019s Touch</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Mind 3 and must increase the other Skill she used to meet the requirements of the Legacy to 3, or must attain two dots in a second skill from the list of possible requirements.<br /> The mage learns to weave threads of shared awareness, creating a mental tapestry that connects them to another being. Whit this intimate link forged helping them to navigate the perilous journeys ahead. This act like the Ritual Focus(SoS p55) spell, but instead of working on a particular spell, participants receive their bonus on journeys through the Hedge and the Dreaming Roads. Reach is assigned for advanced duration and target, allowing the mage to affect multiple people.<br /> <b>Optional Fate 3:</b> By manipulating the threads of fate, the mage can shift the odds in their favor. This ability manifests similar to Malleable Thorns(DE2 p377) but instead of automatically hadgespinning something, it allows the mage to spend mana and roll Hedgespinning for the remainder of the scene, with exceptional sucesses allowing for an additional mana to be spent on Paradigm Shits.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 05-22-2024, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-22T11:21:30-07:00","id":1536103,"title":"","content":"My first question here is, why would you need an attainment to get Court Goodwill? And the second is, do you need this Legacy at all for your goal?<br /> <br /> I'm also interested in crossover rules, but unfortunately I'm yet to read CtL 2e. My take on it, though, is to have as much as possible of the crossover happening at the most basic level, so it doesn't lock the character in having to dedicate their build just to be able to participate in the game.<br /> <br /> So, I would make a list of the abilities a character needs to work in Changeling, and then look for the simplest way of giving them access to each.<br /> <br /> Other than that, social groups should be the simplest thing to adapt here, and the crossover should create more options, not less. As per the 1st Ed rules I would let any character get Court Goodwill simply because they make the effort to take part in Court affairs, and maybe create Legacies that represent Court Mantle, or even Entitlements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-22T13:24:29-07:00","id":1536114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed?p=1536103#post1536103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first question here is, why would you need an attainment to get Court Goodwill? And the second is, do you need this Legacy at all for your goal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was thinking about the spell Wyrd backed Oaths that let mages participate in Wyrd Oaths(like the one necessary for joining a changeling court), with this I think the Mage would also have access to Court Goodwill. On 2nd edition, this merit gives some benefits of the Mantle, so I didn't think other Major Splats could get it.<br /> <br /> The goal is not to join a court and get Court Goodwill, but to have that as an option. The objective of this legacy is to allow a mage to travel on the Hedge and on the Dreaming Roads, having access to some options like hedgespinning and bargains with the denizens of those places. It can be accomplished with awakened spells? Sure, but the legacy aims in facilitating it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed?p=1536103#post1536103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than that, social groups should be the simplest thing to adapt here, and the crossover should create more options, not less. As per the 1st Ed rules I would let any character get Court Goodwill simply because they make the effort to take part in Court affairs, and maybe create Legacies that represent Court Mantle, or even Entitlements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I try to not lean too much inside other splats powers. The Hedge is a realm and much of the changeling conflict is tied to it, so I created this legacy for my character to have access to it, but I don't want to create a legacy that let's a mage get the powers of a Contract or the full benefits of Mantles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}